TI  - STUDIES ON TRANSFER OF OMEGA-3 FATTY-ACIDS INTO BOVINE-MILK FAT
T2  - MILCHWISSENSCHAFT-MILK SCIENCE INTERNATIONAL
AB  - A milk fat enriched with omega-3 fatty acids may be of interest for the prevention of cardiovascular disease. It is controversial up to now if and how much of long-cabin polyunsaturated omega-3 fatty acids in marine oils can be utilized by the bovine mammary gland for milk fat synthesis even if they are protected from biohydrogenation by the rumen microflora. Two lactating cows got infusions of 220-420 g menhaden oil per day for 28 or 43 days, respectively. The average depression of milk fat and protein content was 0.5 or less than 0.2%, respectively. The average steady state omega-3 fatty acid content in milk fat following 420 g menhaden oil was 6 weight%. Hence, 35-40% of the infused omega-3 fatty acids were transferred to milk fat under therse conditions. Trans fatty acids content of C18-isomeres was never more than 5 weight%. It is concluded that a surprisingly efficient transifer of long-chain poly-unsaturated fatty acids of marine oils into bovine milk fat is possible.
