TI  - Omega-3 Polyunsaturated Fatty Acids and Mixed Dementia
T2  - 27TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE OF ALZHEIMER'S DISEASE INTERNATIONAL
CP  - 27th International Conference of Alzheimer's Disease International
AB  - We examined the mechanisms of action of omega-3 (n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFAs) in the contexts of both Alzheimer's disease (AD) and vascular dementia (VaD) in order to determine if the use of n-3s could be applicable in regards to mixed dementia (MD). Omega-3 fatty acids may be beneficial to persons with MD by potentially reducing neuroinflammation associated with both AD and VaD symptoms. There is very little research in regards to MD. There are common threads between AD and VaD, and therapies that target these common threads should be explored. Since many persons with dementia exhibit both AD and VaD pathology, such treatments would be extremely beneficial if demonstrated to be efficacious.
