TI  - The scientific basis of the SU.FOL.OM3 study: a secondary intervention trial of folate, B6 and B12 vitamins and/or omega3 falty acid supplements in the prevention of recurrent ischemic events
T2  - SANG THROMBOSE VAISSEAUX
AB  - Cardiovascular diseases are the primary cause of mortality in France. Many epidemiological studies have shown that the total homocysteine concentration (tHcy) is a risk indicator for cardiovascular diseases. Furthermore, it has been shown that tHcy can be effectively lowered by supplementation with folic acid, vitamin B6 and B12. However, it is not yet known whether a reduction of tHcy by such a supplementation indeed leads to a decreased risk of cardiovascular disease. Another possible dietary factor that may lower the risk of cardiovascular disease is fish-oil, which is rich in omega-3 fatty acids. These fatty acids may lower platelet aggregation and triglyceride-rich lipoproteins and may have antiarythmic effects. Some trials have investigated the effect of fish or fish-oil on cardiovascular mortality, but results are inconclusive. In the SUFOLOM3 study, we will therefore evaluate the effect of supplementation of nutritional doses of folic acid supplementation, in combination with vitamin B6 and B12, at nutritional doses and/or supplementation with omega-3 fatty acids on recurrent ischemic diseases in a factorial design. The SUFOLOM3 Study is a randomized double blind, placebo-controlled, secondary-prevention trial. Two thousand five hundred two patients, aged between 45 and 80 years who had a past history of myocardial infarction, unstable angina pectoris or an ischemic stroke have been included. The subjects are supplemented and followed-up for a period of five years. Analysis of results is planned for end of 2009.
