TI  - Nonpharmacologic treatment of hypertriglyceridemia: Focus on fish oils
T2  - CLINICAL CARDIOLOGY
AB  - Early studies in Greenland Eskimos stimulated interest in evaluating the effect of Omega-3 fatty acids on coronary artery disease. Subsequent studies showed a significant decrease in triglyceride levels in patients receiving high doses of fish oil containing DHA and EPA. Slight increases in LDL were also observed in patients receiving fish oil supplements. These studies have also shown a dose-response effect which persists as long as supplementation continues. Later trials, specifically the Diet and Reinfarction Trial and the Indian Experiment of Infarct Survival, have:demonstrated a reduction in cardiac death rates and in the incidence of cardiac symptoms in patients receiving fish oil.
